{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/157688-electrfication-shock-divine-lightning-reflexsive-aggravated-damage","id":157688,"title":"Electrfication - Shock/Divine Lightning: Reflexsive Aggravated damage.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T02:55:20-07:00","id":157688,"title":"Electrfication - Shock/Divine Lightning: Reflexsive Aggravated damage.","content":"So something just came up recently. Purely according to the rules, a Promethean with the 5-dot Transmutation Divine Lightning, could conceivably activate the Shock part of that Transmutation a any number of times he wished, depending on his Azoth. I'm not gonna go &quot;And with Azoth 10, he could do it 15 times per turn!!!11one!&quot;, but it isn't wholly unrealistic for a PC to have an Azoth score of 3-4 or even 5, and that would yield 3, 4 and 5 activations respectively. That's a lot of damage, when you roll Azoth+Stamina, and inflict Aggravated damage on anyone unfortunate to stand next to you. And its a <i>Reflexsive Action </i>meaning you could concievably activate another Transmutation or just punch somebody in the face, in <i>addition</i> to doing like 15 Aggravated damage.<br /> And <i>on top of that</i>, they have to roll to avoid getting stunned out of their next turn, in which the Promethean can just repead the Shock-O-Rama as needed, untill he is out of Pyros. But by then, the enemy is probably reduced to a smoldering heap of flesh on the ground...<br /> <br /> I am by no means saying that it <i>should</i> function this way, but from what I can gather, if one goes purely by the books, it does. If I ever ran a Promethean quest, I'de probably nerf it some, but I was curious if I'de understood it properly, or anyone had come up with interesting Hacks for this particular power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:10:09-07:00","id":158182,"title":"","content":"I always understood the power as upgrading Shock/Arc; activating that <i>upgrade</i> is Reflexive. The actual attacks are still Instant.<br /> Also, they're attacks, of which you only get one.<br /> Yes, this is poorly written rules. I'll re-read it after work to see if I understand properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:14:55-07:00","id":158275,"title":"","content":"Yes. For the normal shock, I agree with you. That Transmutation has Reflexsive as its action too, but those rules specifically say, that you need to touch the target first. So it makes sense in that context, that since you need to touch first, you cant touch an enemy multiple times, so you only get one activation.<br /> However, for the Divine Lightning variant of the Shock Transmutation, that limitation is removed. That Transmutation dosen't require you to touch the target, just to stand close enough. It creates a kind of lightning storm around you, of varing size depending on how high your Azoth score is. And since that lightning storm dosen't require you to touch the victim, you should concievably be able to activate it as many times as you have Azoth/Pyros to.<br /> Thats my rationale for the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}